<content><![CDATA[<p>Final project brief (student-defined, theme-driven); proposal presentations; critical perspectives on digital fabrication.</p><h2>Ideas</h2><p>Critical making (Ratto); the maker movement and its critics (Morozov); open hardware, sharing files, and the politics of making; sustainability.</p><h2>In class</h2><ul><li>Lecture/discussion (50 min)</li><li>proposal pitches (80 min)</li><li>planning (40 min)</li></ul>]]></content>
